(2) Points A-6/A-7 (structure) and the project's region-naming requirement —
each region's accessible name is "<card h2> chart data" and unique; Tab from
<summary> reaches the region; table keeps <th scope="col"> + caption:
  h2 text per chart-container (evaluated in-page):
    ["Budget vs Actual Over Time","Spending by Major Expense",
     "Spending Trend","Top Spending","Cumulative Balance"]
  role=region aria-labels (branch, all 4 combos, identical):
    ["Budget vs Actual Over Time chart data","Spending by Major Expense chart data",
     "Spending Trend chart data","Top Spending chart data",
     "Cumulative Balance chart data"]
  → each label is exactly "<h2 text> chart data"; all 5 distinct (set size 5).
  Keyboard probe (tabprobe.js): focused the first chart's <summary>, pressed
  Enter to open, pressed Tab once →
    activeElement = {"tag":"DIV","role":"region",
      "ariaLabel":"Budget vs Actual Over Time chart data","tabIndex":0}
  i.e. Tab from the <summary> lands on the region as the very next stop.
  Table structure (tablestruct.js) inside the wrapper:
    caption: "Values as plotted; the rows show this chart's category and
      time scope. Negative values retain their sign."
    th[scope]: ["col","col","col"] for Series / Period or category / Value
  — caption and <th scope="col"> unchanged by this task (the diff never
  touches those lines).
  Total role="region" landmarks on /dashboard: 5, all inside closed-by-default
  <details>. OBSERVATION: five nested named regions is more landmark surface
  than the page had before, but ACCESSIBILITY.md does not prohibit
  region-per-disclosure and each has a distinct, descriptive name (not a
  "region"/"region 2" collision) — judged acceptable, flagged for the lead
  as a landmark-count note rather than a failure, per WCAG 2.2 AA (which sets
  no numeric landmark ceiling) and A-6 (silent on this specific case).

(3) Persistence across an HTMX range-change replot (tabprobe.js): captured
aria-label list before clicking a #date-filter-form preset button, then again
after the HTMX swap + Plotly replot settled (waited for
`#chart-major-expense?.data?.length` then +800ms):
  before: ["Budget vs Actual Over Time chart data", ... 5 total]
  after:  identical 5 labels, each still {tabIndex:0, role:"region"}
Confirms the attributes are re-set on every `updateTable()` run (the
assignment lines sit unconditionally inside the function body, executed both
by the MutationObserver callback and the `plotly_afterplot` listener wired up
inside that same observer callback) — they are not a one-time DOM write that
a re-plot could clobber.

(4) Point A-16-equivalent / progressive enhancement — with JS off, the
details/tables do not exist; server placeholder unchanged vs master:
