FAILURES: none.

OBSERVATIONS (non-blocking):
- Five newly-focusable/named regions on /dashboard when all disclosures are
  open is more landmark surface than master; each has a distinct name so it
  is not the "ambiguous region" anti-pattern, but if the lead later wants to
  quiet the landmark tree (e.g. only exposing role=region while the
  <details> is open, which is already true since focus/DOM order lives
  inside the collapsed <details> and axe scanned with them forced open) that
  would be a design choice, not an accessibility defect under
